{
  "id": "shakti-alternate",
  "name": "8 Coil Shakti style (fast channel alternation)",
  "category": "spiritual",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "origin": "Todd Murphy, 8 Coil Shakti (consumer descendant of the Persinger/Koren lab helmets)",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "The 8 Coil Shakti's standard temporal set-up: a 4-coil cross on each temporal lobe and the amygdala burst-firing signal, switching every half-second between the top-and-bottom coils and the front-and-back coils of both crosses (the vendor's \"fast\" alternation), for 30 min.",
  "notes": "The 8 Coil Shakti puts a cross on each temporal lobe (top, bottom, front and back; about C5, T9, FT7, TP7 and C6, T10, FT8, TP8; the site names are an inference). One stereo channel drives the top and bottom coils of both crosses, the other the front and back coils, and in \"fast\" mode the signal switches channels every half-second, which the vendor says emerged as \"the most effective\" in the original developers' lab tests (\"slow\" mode switches once per signal). Here two tracks, each with the signal gated in a point table, reproduce that switch; so that the half-second clock and the signal repeat together, a burst comes every 4.5 s (3.8 s of silence instead of about 4 s), and successive bursts start on alternate coil pairs. As on the vendor's coil chart, each pair is one + and one - coil: C5 (top) and FT7 (front) on the left and T10 (bottom) and TP8 (back) on the right get the reversed signal (weight -1), while T9, TP7, C6 and FT8 get it as is. The amygdala ('burstx') file is proprietary and is approximated by the built-in accelerating burst (6 to 30 Hz, 230 points of 3 ms = 0.69 s). The vendor's session lengths are 10 (tests), 20, 30 or 60 min; 30 min is the length for a series. Murphy's seizure anecdote involved left/right attention shifting in a seizure-prone person: skip this preset with any seizure history, and also with a psychiatric diagnosis or medication or migraine. An independent randomized, sham-controlled test of the 8 Coil Shakti amygdala signal over both temporal lobes (30 min, 37 people) found no effect on emotional responses (Gendle & McGrath 2012); Murphy disputes their choice of session. Granqvist 2005 also found no field effect. Persinger's lab reported more aggression and less trust after three weekly bilateral burst-firing sessions (Gillis & Persinger 1993): stop if you notice irritability.",
  "setting": "For effects during the session: darkness and acoustic silence (blindfold and earplugs; Murphy says white noise is no substitute). Otherwise any quiet room.",
  "schedule": "At most weekly or every 72 h, never on consecutive days; series of 3 or 6, then a 21-day break.",
  "targets": ["left-amygdala", "right-amygdala", "left-superior-temporal-gyrus-posterior", "right-superior-temporal-gyrus-posterior"],
  "source": "Murphy, 8 Coil Shakti https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/rotating/index.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Getting started (8-coil chart) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/getting_started_basic.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: 8 coil placement https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/8_coil_placement.htm ; Murphy, Understanding the 8 Coil Shakti (fast and slow alternation) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rot_principles.htm ; Murphy, Using the 8 Coil Shakti over the temporal lobes https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rot_temporal.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: How long should sessions be https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/safe_durations.htm ; Murphy, Enlightenment lecture https://youtu.be/zqrpKUTMXgY?t=4417 ; Gendle & McGrath 2012, Percept Mot Skills 114:217 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22582690/ ; Murphy, A reply to Gendle & McGrath http://www.innerworlds.50megs.com/Gendle_Shakti/8-Coil-Shakti-Gendle-&-McGrath.htm ; Gillis & Persinger 1993, Percept Mot Skills 76:168 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8451123/ ; Granqvist et al. 2005, Neurosci Lett 379:1 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15849873/",
